From 05da99d472f86611a96151ef515664b70ba765d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:02:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] CameraDeviceImpl: null-check
 multiResConcurrentReadersInfo

Second capture-session crash this round, right after the configureStreams
fix let preview actually start:

  E AndroidRuntime: FATAL EXCEPTION: CameraDeviceExecutor
  java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to get length of null array
      at CameraDeviceImpl$CameraDeviceCallbacks.sendOnMultiResolutionOutputStarted(CameraDeviceImpl.java:2808)

sendOnMultiResolutionOutputStarted() only bails out when
Flags.multiResolutionConcurrentReaders() is disabled, then
unconditionally for-eaches over the multiResConcurrentReadersInfo
array. That flag defaults to enabled, but
CaptureResultExtras.multiResConcurrentReadersStartInfo has no default
value and the legacy (Camera1-backed) capture path that builds
CaptureResultExtras for this device's HAL never populates it, so it's
null on every single capture on this device - there's no way for a
legacy-shimmed camera to have a MultiResolutionImageReader in the
first place. Add a null check next to the existing flag check and bail
out the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I11e2abce4f11f2c3a77ed826a1068d0a678e0267
---
 .../android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraDeviceImpl.java    | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraDeviceImpl.java b/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraDeviceImpl.java
index c0640359c848..13f53802b8c7 100644
--- a/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraDeviceImpl.java
+++ b/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraDeviceImpl.java
@@ -2803,6 +2803,13 @@ public class CameraDeviceImpl extends CameraDevice
             if (!Flags.multiResolutionConcurrentReaders()) {
                 return;
             }
+            // The legacy (Camera1-backed) capture path builds its own CaptureResultExtras
+            // without ever populating this new field, so it stays null there even though the
+            // flag defaults to enabled; there's nothing to report for a device that can't have
+            // MultiResolutionImageReaders in the first place.
+            if (multiResConcurrentReadersInfo == null) {
+                return;
+            }
             // Iterate through all MultiResolutionImageReaders' concurrent start info, and send
             // callbacks.
             for (MultiResConcurrentReadersStartInfo info : multiResConcurrentReadersInfo) {
